# Copy to .envrc.local (gitignored) and fill in, then run `direnv allow`.
#
# A project-scoped Cloudflare API token. With this set, wrangler ignores the global
# `wrangler login` entirely, so this project's deploys are unaffected by work on any other
# project — which is the whole point.
#
# Create at: https://dash.cloudflare.com/profile/api-tokens → Create Token
# Start from the "Edit Cloudflare Workers" template, then scope it to the
# media@shaheedibunga.com account only. Add D1:Edit if/when the data layer moves to D1.
#
# Least privilege matters here: this repository is public and the app handles children's
# data. Do not reuse an account-wide token.

# export CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN="…"
